    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm trying to get some info for my shop. we're a small manufacturing outfit and i'm seeing a lot of news about these new EPA carbon emission mandates. what are the actual consequences of these mandates for small-scale industrial manufacturers like us?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "These new EPA mandates primarily target large facilities and stationary sources, so small-scale manufacturers with low annual emissions often face minimal direct requirements. However, you will likely need to update your energy monitoring systems to track baseline usage accurately. Additionally, consumer perception and eligibility for certain federal grants may shift if your facility's visibility increases or if you choose to audit voluntarily for future industry standards. Consulting with an environmental specialist familiar with small business exemptions is highly recommended before investing in compliance infrastructure.",
